From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 9/12] wifi: mt76: mt7615: load and unload a part whose firmware owns the MAC

On a part whose firmware owns the MAC:

  - load the ROM patch at its own address and both RAM images through
    the shared code, the CR4 image split into regions like the N9 one
  - take readiness from the host interface: MT_TOP_MISC2_FW_N9_RDY stays
    clear
  - send only the calibration window of the EEPROM file, and read the
    MAC address from the efuse through the firmware, falling back to a
    random one, since the file's is the same on every unit
  - run the firmware before registration, which the address needs, and
    set the offload capabilities before registering
  - refuse a firmware left running at probe, and on unload power it
    down and hand ownership back, so a reload needs no power cycle
  - receive its events on the second receive queue

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
